# XILINDRO alone, a loss: no key at all. The opponent walks in, attacks
# from up to 130 px and jumps back, every 6-7 beats (about 1.3 s), and the
# fighter, on guard, takes every blow: its energy is below 1 at about 35 s
# and 31 end ticks later the window closes with a loss of -1000, at 39700
# (Original) or 101150 (`--fix all`: the easy opponent, below).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame xilindro --headless --ms 42000 --input tools/play/xilindro-alone-lose.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame xilindro --headless --ms 105000 --fix all --input tools/play/xilindro-alone-lose.input
# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows XILINDRO's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
50 ?fight_controls_screen key return
50 ?fight_controls_screen delay 2050
20000 dump fight
37000 dump lost
41000 !fight_controls_screen result lost -1000
# The Corrigida's fight (`fight_fair`, `fight_easy_ai`: docs/fights/FAIRNESS.md,
# EASY_AI.md) takes longer: the opponent telegraphs, dithers, waits and guards,
# so the fighter is not knocked out and the 90-s clock ends it, 91 to 29 or so;
# the window closes at 101150.
0 ?fight_fair delay 52000
48000 ?fight_controls_screen result lost -1000
